Dear OCaml users,=20

We have the pleasure of celebrating the birthday of Giovanni Girolamo Sacch=
eri=20
by announcing the release of OCaml version 5.5.1.=20

This patch-level release fixes a major type system bug for module-dependent=
=20
functions and also contains two security fixes for the runtime: one in the=
=20
Marshal module, another inside the loading of bytecode.=20

At a less severe level, this release also fixes two bugs in the runtime for=
=20
concurrent programs, another runtime bug for musl users; and a handful of o=
ther=20
bugs.=20

The release also restores support for cloning the compiler on macOS.=20

Overall, we are strongly advising you to switch to OCaml 5.5.1 if you were=
=20
already using OCaml 5.5.0.=20

The full list of bug fixes is available below for more details.=20

Happy hacking,=20
-- Florian Angeletti, for the OCaml team.=20

Installation Instructions=20
-------------------------------=20

The base compiler can be installed as an opam switch with the following com=
mands:=20

opam update=20
opam switch create 5.5.1=20

The source code for the release is also directly available on:=20

* GitHub: https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/archive/5.5.1.tar.gz)=20
* Inria archive: https://caml.inria.fr/pub/distrib/ocaml-5.5/ocaml-5.5.1.ta=
r.gz=20

Changes compared to 5.5.0=20
-------------------------------------=20

### Type system=20

- [14891](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14891), [14982](https://git=
hub.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14982): fix scope error leading to an erroneous =
typechecking for=20
non-dependent application of module-dependent function in presence of=20
dependent first-class module types:=20
```ocaml=20
module type T =3D sig module type S end=20
let f (module M:T) (m: (module M.S)) =3D m=20
module type P =3D sig type 'a t end=20
let error =3D=20
f (module struct module type S =3D P end) (module List)=20
````=20
(Florian Angeletti, report by Hazem ElMasry, review by Gabriel Scherer)=20

### Runtime=20

- [14872](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14872): harden loading of b=
ytecode executable files against corrupted=20
or malicious files having 2^29 TOC entries or more.=20
(Xavier Leroy, review by Nicol=E1s Ojeda B=E4r)=20

- [15019](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15019): `Marshal.from_{stri=
ng,bytes}`: guard against overflow in=20
the computation of the total data length.=20
(Xavier Leroy, report by Akshay Singh, review by Nicol=E1s Ojeda B=E4r=20
and Antonin D=E9cimo)=20

- [14933](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14933): Respect `sysconf(_S=
C_SIGSTKSZ)` when choosing the size for the=20
alternate signal stack, avoiding fatal errors when linked against musl libc=
 on=20
some Intel CPUs.=20
(Nat Mote, review by Florian Angeletti and Miod Vallat)=20

- [14940](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14940), fix a memory leak i=
n the OCaml runtime by bounding the size=20
of the internal cache of stacks.=20
(Vesa Karvonen, Florian Angeletti, review by Gabriel Scherer)=20

- [15029](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15029): Fix a regression on=
 Windows where an OCaml thread that never=20
yielded voluntarily would keep the runtime lock forever, so that the other=
=20
threads of its domain never ran. Preemptive switching between systhreads ha=
d=20
no effect; only explicit calls to `Thread.yield` or blocking sections would=
=20
let other threads run.=20
(Nicol=E1s Ojeda B=E4r, report by Daniel Larraz, review by Antonin D=E9cimo=
)=20

### Build system=20

- [14883](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14883), [14884](https://git=
hub.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14884): fix Windows cross-compilation with older=
 mingw32-gcc versions=20
(Brian Ward, review by Antonin D=E9cimo and Stefan Muenzel)=20

- [14871](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14871), [14914](https://git=
hub.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14914): Ignore OCAMLTOP_INCLUDE_PATH during the =
build.=20
(David Allsopp, report by Andreas Rossberg, review by Florian Angeletti)=20

- [14901](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14901), [14923](https://git=
hub.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14923): Fix the generated installation script to=
 cope with macOS's=20
geriatric version of bash when executing in opam's sandbox.=20
(David Allsopp, report by Julian Fondren and Sacha-=C9lie Ayoun, investigat=
ion=20
and initial fix by Kate Deplaix, review by Florian Angeletti)=20

- [14989](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14989): Improve build repro=
ducibility by letting only otherlibs/{str,unix}=20
build their own .cmi and .cmx. The generic %.cmi/%.cmx rules of the root=20
Makefile were racing with them under make -j and recorded a different sourc=
e=20
path, which changed the interface digest (and, through it, most other compi=
led=20
artefacts) as well as the debug info packed into str.a and unix.a.=20
(Bernhard M. Wiedemann, review by David Allsopp and Stefan Muenzel)=20

### User interface=20

- [14881](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14881), [14882](https://git=
hub.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14882): fix printing of external types that are =
subject to module=20
constraints.=20
(Stefan Muenzel, review by Florian Angeletti)=20

### Runtime events library=20

- [14966](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14966): add the missing EV_=
MINOR_EPHE_CLEAN constructor to=20
Runtime_events.runtime_phase, introduced in [13643](https://github.com/ocam=
l/ocaml/issues/13643). The runtime has emitted=20
this phase since 5.4, when a minor collection has to clean locked ephemeron=
s,=20
but the OCaml type had no constructor for it, so consumers were handed an=
=20
out-of-range value and crashed when matching on it.=20
(Tim McGilchrist, review by Florian Angeletti)=20

- [14969](https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/14969): Fix the units of th=
e runtime events counter EV_C_MINOR_ALLOCATED_WORDS=20
to report as the number of words of minor heap consumed, including headers.=
=20
(Tim McGilchrist, review by Nicol=E1s Ojeda B=E4r)=20



